PATCH 638: keep the FILEMGR DTA in its original module buffer (board:0009).

Actual original2b:a88 MOV EDX,080b /a8d MOV [927],EDX initializes a
logical module offset, not a host pointer outside guest RAM. Source whole
16-MiB/GP/segment/control/raw+lazyflag proof and the natural6032 DWORD
operand provenance are in tools/oracle/detail_loader_case.json. Replace
native_main's host-only buffer with that observed offset. Keep the DWORD
value intact; translate it through the existing fist_ext_addr owner only
when dereferencing the DTA +1a field. Both reads and resource-member
writes need this resolution; actual604a/7038/6397 load [927] and address
[EBX+1a]. Ghidra duplicates the member-size store in its resource paths.

The real6032/5cc2/5d50/DOS regression reaches four parent failures using
that actual module-offset input: Native invalid-address reads and WASM
unrelated-memory query sizes for HIGH.DTL and DSOUNDS.BIN. Existing
host-pointer operand cases retain their prior count/content expectations.
All files are isolated under /tmp. This accepts DTA storage/addressing
only, not resource archive parsing, CF/error paths, full GP/register
transport, original instructions/IRQ/device time or whole frame/PCM parity.
